  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLIMATE CHANGE ADAPTATION AND MITIGATION THROUGH IMPROVED ACCESS TO QUALITY WEATHER INFORMATION, ECOLOGICAL MANAGEMENT AND SUSTAINABLE CLIMATE-RESILIE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">implemented by Against Hunger (ACF) in collaboration with the Ministry of Agriculture and Food Security (MAFS) and the Sierra Leone Meteorological Agency (SLMet). The project aim is to contribute to climate change mitigation and adaptation at community level through the adoption of sustainable food production and ecosystem management systems, advocacy and access to timely and accurate weather information and directly targets 900 farmers (30 FBOs: 30 members per group with 60% female representation) in Jong and Imperri chiefdoms, Bonthe district, Sierra Leone.</narrative>
  </description>
